This plugin vendors three skills from Matt Pocock's "Skills for Real Engineers":

    https://github.com/mattpocock/skills

    skills/engineering/grill-with-docs   -> skills/grill-with-docs
    skills/productivity/grilling         -> skills/grilling
    skills/engineering/domain-modeling   -> skills/domain-modeling

Upstream commit:

    5b15a47f2d7150f545fbcacbfe381787fc0230dc

Only these three are vendored: `grill-with-docs` runs `grilling` with `domain-modeling`,
so the three are the minimal closure. The rest of upstream is deliberately not carried.

LOCAL MODIFICATIONS
-------------------

These files are NOT verbatim. Four patches apply on top of upstream, in this order:

    patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
        Lowercases CONTEXT.md, ADR-FORMAT.md and CONTEXT-FORMAT.md in domain-modeling, so
        a case-sensitive filesystem never holds two competing copies of one doc.
    patches/0002-conditional-round-delivery.patch
        Delivers a grilling round through AskUserQuestion when the tool exists, and as one
        numbered question per turn when it does not (Codex), instead of a prose block. It
        also tells grill-with-docs to read its two siblings when there is no Skill tool,
        and flips allow_implicit_invocation to true in grill-with-docs/agents/openai.yaml.
    patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
        Removes the context-map.md mechanism from domain-modeling, because the `## Contexts`
        section of a repo's AGENTS.md is the map here.
    patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch
        Drops `disable-model-invocation: true` from grill-with-docs, so the model can invoke
        it. This is the Claude half of the openai.yaml change in 0002.

Each patch assumes the ones before it: 0003 deletes lines in the spelling 0001 gave them,
and 0004's context is the sentence 0002 wrote.

RE-SYNCING
----------

    1. Copy the three upstream directories over skills/
    2. git apply patches/0001-lowercase-doc-filenames.patch
    3. git apply patches/0002-conditional-round-delivery.patch
    4. git apply patches/0003-drop-context-map.patch
    5. git apply patches/0004-enable-model-invocation.patch
    6. Update the commit SHA above; regenerate any patch that stops applying

The patches are ordinary `git diff` output with `a/plugins/grill/skills/...` paths, so
apply them from the repo root. To regenerate one, commit the state it applies to, redo the
change on top of that, and `git diff -M` the two commits. Verify the whole chain by
applying it to a fresh copy of upstream in a scratch directory and diffing the result
against skills/. They must be byte-identical.

